---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TrustStrip from '../../components/TrustStrip.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTABand from '../../components/CTABand.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/FAQAccordion.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can my existing wiring support a newer charger?",
    "answer": "In most cases yes. If your existing circuit has properly sized conductors and a compatible breaker, we can mount the new unit on the existing infrastructure after verifying wire condition and terminal integrity."
  },
  {
    "question": "How long does a replacement take?",
    "answer": "A straightforward replacement on existing wiring typically takes 2 to 3 hours, including removal of the old unit, inspection, installation, and live-load testing."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should I do with the old charger?",
    "answer": "We can remove and dispose of the old unit, or you can keep it. If the old charger has recyclable components, we can advise on proper disposal channels."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will a newer charger charge faster?",
    "answer": "If your existing circuit supports higher amperage (e.g., upgrading from a 32A to a 48A unit on a 60A breaker), yes. Otherwise, charging speed is limited by the existing circuit capacity."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I upgrade from plug-in to hardwired during replacement?",
    "answer": "Yes. Converting from a NEMA 14-50 plug-in to a direct hardwired connection during replacement is a common upgrade that improves reliability and enables higher charging speeds."
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title="EV Charger Replacement in Issaquah, WA | Upgrade Your EVSE"
  description="EV charger replacement and upgrade service in Issaquah WA. Swap outdated or damaged units with modern smart charging stations. Call (425) 380-0019."
  canonicalPath="/services/ev-charger-replacement/"
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: '/services/' },
    { name: 'EV Charger Replacement' }
  ]} />

  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width: 840px;">
        <span class="section-tag" style="background: rgba(132, 204, 22, 0.2); color: #84cc16;">Specialized EV Service</span>
        <h1>EV Charger Replacement & Upgrade Service in Issaquah</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">When your charging station is damaged beyond repair, discontinued by the manufacturer, or simply outdated, we remove the old unit and install a modern replacement on your existing electrical infrastructure.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta-wrap">
          <a href="tel:+14253800019" class="btn btn-lime"><span>📞</span><span>Call (425) 380-0019</span></a>
          <a href="/locations/" class="btn btn-outline-white">View All 15 Service Areas</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <TrustStrip />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="rich-content" style="max-width: 900px; margin-inline: auto;">
        <h2>What This Service Covers</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Safe disconnection and removal of the existing EVSE unit</li>
          <li>Inspection of existing wiring, conduit, and breaker for reusability</li>
          <li>Installation of new replacement charging station on existing circuit</li>
          <li>Re-termination and torque verification of all wire connections</li>
          <li>Configuration of new unit settings (amperage, Wi-Fi, scheduling)</li>
          <li>Updated permit filing if required by circuit modifications</li>
        </ul>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/modern-issaquah-garage-ev-charger.jpg" 
            alt="Replacing outdated EV charger with modern smart Level 2 station in Issaquah WA"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Upgrading older, sluggish, or unrepairable charging units to modern high-efficiency smart stations.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <h2>Technical Background & How It Works</h2>
        <p>Charging station technology has advanced rapidly. Units installed five to seven years ago may lack Wi-Fi connectivity, smart scheduling, dynamic load management, or compatibility with newer vehicle charging standards like NACS.</p>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/tesla-wall-connector-repair-installation.jpg" 
            alt="Upgraded Tesla Wall Connector replacing older faulty charger in Issaquah 98029 garage"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Faster charging speeds, Wi-Fi load monitoring, and smartphone app control with modern hardware.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <p>A replacement installation often reuses the existing dedicated circuit, breaker, and conduit, saving significant labor and material costs compared to a full new installation. We verify that existing wiring meets current code requirements and is in sound condition before connecting the new unit.</p>

        <p>This service is available throughout all 15 Issaquah neighborhoods, including <a href="/locations/issaquah-highlands/">Issaquah Highlands</a>, <a href="/locations/talus/">Talus</a>, <a href="/locations/klahanie/">Klahanie</a>, and <a href="/locations/olde-town-issaquah/">Olde Town Issaquah</a>. Browse our full <a href="/locations/">locations hub</a> to find your area.</p>

        <h2>When to Contact Us</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Your charger is damaged beyond economical repair</li>
          <li>The manufacturer discontinued your charger model and parts are unavailable</li>
          <li>You want to upgrade from an older charger to a modern smart unit</li>
          <li>Your charger lacks features you need (Wi-Fi, load sharing, NACS)</li>
          <li>You are switching vehicle brands and need a different charger type</li>
        </ul>

        <figure class="seo-service-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
          <img 
            src="/images/panel-upgrade-200-amp-circuit-breakers.jpg" 
            alt="Electrician adapting existing circuit wiring for high-amperage replacement charger"
            width="900"
            height="500"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 440px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);"
          />
          <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.65rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
            Reusing existing conduit and conductors where compliant to minimize replacement costs.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>


        <p>For technical questions about ev charger replacement in Issaquah, call our dispatch line directly at <a href="tel:+14253800019">(425) 380-0019</a>. Licensed under <a href="https://apps.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=296-46B" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WAC 296-46B</a> and fully compliant with NEC Article 625 standards.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FAQAccordion items={faqs} />

  <section class="section" style="background: #ffffff; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-bottom: 1px solid #e2e8f0;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title-wrap">
        <span class="section-tag">Related Solutions</span>
        <h2>Related EV Charging Services</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <h3 class="card-title">EV Charger Troubleshooting</h3>
          <a href="/services/ev-charger-troubleshooting/" class="card-link">View Service Details →</a>
